From f9af7986dbc44be8e64a8adbf6a48bdaee865971 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: homar <homar@local>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 14:13:32 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] homalawn computers: the link knows the calling computer; Pins
 is a list with last seen and forget tombstones

Every link command now carries the calling computer's fingerprint. Pins keeps name, added and
last seen (written at most once a minute) per computer, lists them, and forget() removes one,
leaves a tombstone (newest 64) and tells the removal listeners; a computer that unpairs itself
leaves no tombstone but also notifies the listeners. Pairing again clears the tombstone. An
unpaired hello and the not_paired error say "forgotten" for a tombstoned computer. Debug hooks
debug_computers and debug_forget.
